This is dope. Let's go.

236
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:53,485
- Look at them high-fiving already.
- Anything water-related, they're in.

237
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:55,904
- "Anything water-related."
- So true!

238
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:59,824
SAUNA

239
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:02,827
Whoa, wait, wait, wait.
This place looks kind of familiar.

240
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:04,829
Kazuma, go jump in first.

241
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:07,290
- Isn't it too soon?
- Can we just go in?

242
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:09,834
- Okay, let's do it.
- Open the door!

243
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:11,796
- All right.
- It's boiling!

244
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,214
- Watch your head.
- So hot!

245
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:16,341
- I'm on fire!
- This is extra intense.

246
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:18,177
- Sit down.
- This is the best!

247
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:21,680
I have a question. How was it with her?

248
00:11:21,681 --> 00:11:22,972
Good question.

249
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,265
- Go on.
- We shared a bed.

250
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:26,142
- Nice.
- What about… Did you…

251
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:27,602
- No, we didn't.
- You didn't?

252
00:11:27,603 --> 00:11:29,479
- You really didn't?
- No, we didn't.

253
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,398
- You were a gentleman?
- That's right.

254
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:32,982
- Yeah?
- She fall asleep in your arms?

255
00:11:32,983 --> 00:11:34,150
- That's all.
- Respect.

256
00:11:34,151 --> 00:11:37,488
Get out of here with that cool guy act.
He's trying hard to play it cool.

257
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,948
I was the only one who bet you'd kiss her.

258
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:40,865
Really?

259
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,868
He's not in a position to say that!

260
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:46,621
Seriously, why tempt fate like that,
you know?

261
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:49,332
Rune and I talked about this,
actually, remember?

262
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,291
Oh, yeah, we did.

263
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:53,545
He was like, "If she wants it,
I'm ready to make a move."

264
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:55,964
- I had 1,000 opportunities last night.
- Oh, for real?

265
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:58,508
Like, while we were drinking,
she'd shift her body a little,

266
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:00,719
and suddenly, she's this close to my face.

267
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,636
Right.

268
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:04,305
- But I was like, "Not the right time."
- Know what?

269
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:07,100
I can see you ordering nonstop champagne
at a hostess bar.

270
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:08,935
You're an easy target.

271
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:11,896
- I'll keep myself under control there.
- That's impressive.

272
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:15,066
At Mimi's club, you'd be ordering
and popping bottles nonstop.

273
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:16,985
I would've kissed her if it were me.

274
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,027
- You would?
- Me too.

275
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,571
Kazuma would lose his nerve.

276
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:22,282
- Think I'd chicken out?
- No way I'm telling you.

277
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,243
- This thing goes by so fast.
- It's over before you know it.

278
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:27,704
- Seriously, so fast.
- Tai-chan, you're not done yet, right?

279
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:29,456
- You're gonna flunk again.
- Again?

280
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:31,708
- Nah, I've had enough.
- You'll be on round three.

281
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:34,085
- Don't worry, I'll stay with you.
- No way.

282
00:12:34,086 --> 00:12:36,546
Wait, are you going bald?

283
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:37,964
- Am I?
- Must be the stress.

284
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,007
Am I really?

285
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:41,760
But honestly, I'm glad I stayed here.
Glad I got the chance, you know?

286
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:44,554
For me, it's not even
just about finding love anymore.

287
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:46,681
- I feel like I've grown as a person.
- I feel the same way.

288
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:48,058
- Yeah, you know?
- Seriously.

289
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,978
- Ready to go?
- To the ocean? Let's do it.

290
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:53,605
- Hell yeah!
- Go.

291
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:55,482
Argh, I'm cooked.

292
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,691
- Let's take a dip.
- It's hot!

293
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,902
- So hot!
- Ryopi, your sandals!

294
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:00,278
Here we go!

295
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:01,780
- Yeah!
- No!

296
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:03,615
Oh, man. Whoa, it's so shallow.

297
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,492
- Whoa!
- This feels so damn good.

298
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:08,369
- <i>A cold bath. I bet that's nice.</i>
- <i>This looks like so much fun.</i>

299
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:10,289
Whoa!

300
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,291
- Hell yeah!
- This is awesome!

301
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:14,919
- Holy cow, that's good!
- So nice.

302
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:18,546
- This is the best!
- Man, this is amazing.

303
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:20,048
- God!
- Unreal!

304
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:22,091
- Beautiful, right?
- This is so dope.

305
00:13:22,092 --> 00:13:24,053
- Sun's shining.
- Incredible.

306
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:29,058
Let's huddle up.

307
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:32,393
- Let's go, you bastards!
- Let's go!

308
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:34,437
Never give up!

309
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:36,356
Together, we can all win!

310
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:37,649
You hear me?

311
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:40,068
We busted our asses to get here!

312
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:42,946
Here we go, boys!

313
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,198
What are we even doing?

314
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,202
That's such a beautiful shot.

315
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:51,454
- Hurray for the damn water.
- Yep, hurray.

316
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:54,208
"Hurray for the damn water."
Hurray to the water indeed.

317
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:58,878
It's the final stretch now.
We gotta give it our all.

318
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,088
Mmm-hmm.

319
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:03,091
Just all went by in a flash.
I blinked, it's almost over.

320
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:05,385
Me and Ryopi haven't been on one date yet.

321
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:07,095
- True.
- I really want to.

322
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:10,348
What even is a date, you know?
What does romance really mean?

323
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:11,891
That's deep.

324
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,310
Not really. It was shallow.

325
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:16,396
<i>Another beautiful shot.</i>

326
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:18,773
- They were fighting five minutes ago.
- Unbelievable.

327
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:20,441
Then jumped into the ocean.

328
00:14:20,442 --> 00:14:22,569
Then suddenly, all these tough guys
are laying in the sun.

329
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:24,612
- I know.
- Using each other as pillows.

330
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:27,116
- Aw. That's youth.
- "What does romance even mean?"

331
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,492
Can we send them home now or what?

332
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:31,870
I mean, I think they bonded.

333
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,162
Speaking of bonding,

334
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:37,000
I've been thinking about Rune
and how, in his interview about Mimi,

335
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:40,087
he was saying over and over
how he had so much fun that night.

336
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:43,172
But the fact he snapped that hard
makes me think

337
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:45,633
maybe he was actually frustrated that

338
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:48,553
he couldn't get as close to Mimi
as he was hoping.

339
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:51,306
- Yeah.
- And wanted to blame someone for that.

340
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:54,935
Like, "You guys butted in right when
we wanted to focus on each other."

341
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,688
- You have your gym shoes?
- Shoot, I left mine.

342
00:14:58,689 --> 00:15:00,732
Here, can I have the ball?

343
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,317
RINRIN (20)
HOSTESS

344
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,193
<i>Of course. They're the same age.</i>

345
00:15:04,194 --> 00:15:06,280
- <i>The exact same age.</i>
- <i>That's right.</i>

346
00:15:07,197 --> 00:15:08,239
KAHOCHI (20)
HOSTESS

347
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,743
Shooting from this side,
hit the upper-left corner of that square.

348
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:15,372
Whoa. You're like a coach.

349
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:17,333
Look, it's so pretty.

350
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:19,209
Totally.

351
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:23,129
I actually don't think
I'm into anyone here yet, to be honest.

352
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:26,257
- Maybe it'll take time.
- Other than Kazuma, I guess.

353
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:30,178
I mean, who knows, he might be into Sara,
but I can't just do nothing.

354
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,179
Right.

355
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,597
Once things settle down,

356
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:35,141
everyone should come back to Okinawa,
and we can all hang out.

357
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:37,101
- I'd love that.
- Right? Great.

358
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:39,563
- It's nice we're the same age.
- Totally.

359
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:44,567
We were looking out at the ocean, smoking…
and just chatting.

360
00:15:44,568 --> 00:15:47,153
It's so great to have someone my age.

361
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:49,990
I mean, it just makes that person
easier to talk to.

362
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:53,826
For some reason,
all my friends are Capricorns.

363
00:15:53,827 --> 00:15:56,412
Isn't that weird? Kaho's a Capricorn too.

364
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:58,081
Rinrin must be into astrology.

365
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,916
- Don't you agree?
- Yeah, strong opinions on that.

366
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:02,001
By the way, what's your sign, Nagano?

367
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,461
Oh, I'm actually a Virgo.

368
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:04,754
- Oh.
- I see.

369
00:16:04,755 --> 00:16:06,547
I knew you were gonna react that way.

370
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:08,299
I didn't wanna tell you.

371
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,928
We really click.
I don't have to hold back at all.

372
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:14,305
I can be myself with her.

373
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:15,808
Even back in my hometown,

374
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:20,561
I'm one of those people
that only needs a few friends I can trust.

375
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,855
With Kahochi,

376
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:25,692
I feel like I can really see us
being friends later.

377
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,986
She's not just another person
in the group.

378
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,445
I want her around as a friend.

379
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:32,865
Yeah, at the end of the day,
I guess Kahochi means a lot to me now.

380
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:35,785
- <i>Oh, that's good for them.</i>
- <i>Really on the same wavelength.</i>

381
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:36,703
<i>Definitely.</i>

382
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:39,330
Hmm, I don't like
super skinny guys, but that tummy--

383
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:41,708
- He has a good build.
- That tummy, though.

384
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,001
You guys mind if I fart?

385
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:45,712
- You nuts? Jesus, go outside.
- Go for it.

386
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:46,754
Ew!

387
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:48,506
On that note, I'm gonna go smoke.

388
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:51,300
<i>Gotta be kidding.</i>

389
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:54,053
- Stinking up the room.
- Flap your blanket. I bet it's gonna--

390
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:55,930
Wait, stop!

391
00:16:55,931 --> 00:16:57,473
Ugh, I can practically smell it.

392
00:16:57,474 --> 00:17:00,059
Through the screen?

393
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,646
It's that powerful.
I swear I just smelled it.

394
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:08,526
Kahochi's cracking up.
Hey, stop spreading it all over the room!

395
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,862
- I'm going out for a smoke.
- Gosh.

396
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:13,406
- Yeah, I could use a smoke break too.
- It stinks!

397
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,825
- Evacuate.
- Hey!

398
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,580
It reeks!

399
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,503
- Hey.
- Mmm-mmm.

400
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:29,964
- <i>Oh, it's these two.</i>
- <i>The devoted Kazuma.</i>

401
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:31,841
So you guys went into the sauna together?

402
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:33,259
- All of us.
- Just the guys?

403
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,260
Yep.

404
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:37,555
- Did Rune and Tai-chan make up?
- Yeah, those two made up.

405
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:41,350
And Maru apologized too.
Maru was so pissed, wasn't he?

406
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:43,770
Maru was furious, I know.
I was so surprised.

407
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:45,188
- Yeah, me too.
- We all were.

408
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:47,273
I guess that's what he's like
when he loses it.

409
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:50,068
- He was going full beast mode, for real.
- Yeah.

410
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,403
That was nuts.

411
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:54,156
So, are my feelings
getting through to you?

412
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:58,868
I mean, obviously. You know?

413
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:02,080
I mean, aren't we the only people
doing one-on-ones

414
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,207
with the same person every day?

415
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:08,086
Probably. How do you really feel, though?
You wanna talk to the other guys?

416
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,754
Well, yeah, of course I do.

417
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:12,173
Because, like,
we're living together, you know?

418
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:14,175
- Mmm-hmm.
- I do think about it.

419
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:16,094
- You do?
- 'Cause opportunities are running out.

420
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:17,346
Mmm-hmm, mmm.

421
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:21,850
Hmm.

422
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:25,394
So, I don't know what to do with Kazuma.

423
00:18:25,395 --> 00:18:28,314
I can't bring myself
to ask him to come smoke with me.

424
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:29,565
No, you should ask him.

425
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:30,775
AYACHERU (24)
HOSTESS

426
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,276
I tend to be pretty forward.

427
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:33,695
- Really?
- With Maru.

428
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,155
I ask him.

429
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:37,448
- Mmm.
- Yeah.

430
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:39,909
So, yeah, I think
you should definitely ask him.

431
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:40,993
Yeah, you're right.

432
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:44,330
By the way, Maru has someone else
he's pretty interested in too.

433
00:18:44,331 --> 00:18:46,499
- Oh, yeah?
- He's got options.

434
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,960
But, for me, I feel like Maru is special.

435
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,838
I think I really like him.

436
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:54,549
That's why I make sure to tell him
straight up. Like, "Let's go hang out."

437
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,801
Hmm. I guess
I'm just a little shy about it.

438
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,094
- Is that what it is?
- Yeah.

439
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:00,721
I get that.
I've never done that with guys before.

440
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:04,100
Hey, we're just having a quick smoke.

441
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:07,562
And I was telling her I feel like
I can't make bold moves on my own.

442
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:09,438
- Not much time left.
- True.

443
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:10,731
- Yeah.
- No, I know.

444
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:12,608
I think you'll regret it
if you don't go for it.

445
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:14,360
- Mmm.
- I think so too.

446
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:15,529
No doubt about it.

447
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:20,324
<i>Whenever I have
the one-on-one with Kazuma,</i>

448
00:19:20,325 --> 00:19:21,660
<i>he always brings up Sara.</i>

449
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:25,955
I've never been in a situation before
where a guy wouldn't look my way.

450
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:28,291
Never. I'm like, "Are you kidding me?"

451
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:29,584
Come on!

452
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:32,295
<i>Kazuma,
someone's carrying a torch for you.</i>

453
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:34,715
- Yeah?
- Yeah, I get into street fights.

454
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:37,466
Ah, excuse me, guys.

455
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:39,468
- Hey.
- Sorry to interrupt.

456
00:19:39,469 --> 00:19:42,054
- What do you want?
- I'm Ryopi, and I'm here for my interview.

457
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:43,264
Thank you for having me, ma'am.

458
00:19:43,265 --> 00:19:46,058
- Have a seat and wait your turn.
- Come on, man, don't butt in.

459
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:48,811
- Put a sock in it.
- <i>Ryopi's making his move.</i>

460
00:19:48,812 --> 00:19:51,231
Don't get too flirty, okay?

461
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:54,025
Man, she's cracking up.

462
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:56,694
- That's a hard no.
- She laughs that hard?

463
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:59,780
I'd like to request a change.
Change of hostess!

464
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:01,365
- Why's that?
- She's a nice girl.

465
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:05,204
She laughs like a mad scientist
who's gonna destroy the world.

466
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:07,205
Man, you're funny.

467
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:08,497
Nailed it.

468
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:11,167
- The three of us are like siblings now.
- Right?

469
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:13,212
Yeah. Why do I feel this comfortable?

470
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:18,132
It's funny, we've barely talked until now,
so this feels kind of new, huh?

471
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:19,717
It does. Are you getting butterflies?

472
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:21,677
Huh? I thought that was you.

473
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:23,095
- Whoa.
- Like, is it time?

474
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:25,640
- What do you mean?
- Time for me to move to Okinawa. Duh.

475
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,059
Should I open a bar in Okinawa?

476
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,144
- Could you, please? Do it.
- Yeah, sure.

477
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:32,688
Cool. Do you come to Okinawa a lot?

478
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:34,232
- I do.
- Oh, yeah?

479
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,816
I went to Ta-taki Waterfall.

480
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:37,902
Oh, yeah, the water there feels amazing.

481
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:39,612
- It felt so damn good.
- That place is awesome.

482
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:41,739
At the end, I jumped in
from somewhere super-high.

483
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:42,699
- Like, boing.
- You dived?

484
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:45,034
- Were you okay?
- My nuts hurt bad.

485
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:48,162
- That's rough. That's really gotta hurt.
- I was like, "Oh, my God!"

486
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:50,957
Felt like a baseball bat to the crotch.

487
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:53,209
I bet we're the only ones
talking about crude stuff.

488
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:56,129
Mmm-hmm. Thumbs up from me.

489
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:58,881
- Okay, so, what's your type?
- No.

490
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:01,842
Don't gimme that.
That's not how a conversation works.

491
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:04,512
I asked a Q, so give me an A.
That's what Q&A means!

492
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,472
Let's get a little back and forth going.

493
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:08,683
- Okay, what's your type?
- I don't know.

494
00:21:08,684 --> 00:21:11,687
- We're done here.
- Dead-end conversation.

495
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:15,273
- Seriously, you're the hardest to read.
- I get that a lot.

496
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:17,316
Actually, I get that a lot too.

497
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:19,987
We're just a couple
of unreadable people. Yay!

498
00:21:21,571 --> 00:21:25,032
Well, I mean, I know Kazuma has feelings
for me, so, yeah, you know…

499
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,993
Trust me, you won't find someone
who's that into you.

500
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:28,953
I know. That's definitely true, but…

501
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:31,205
Let me guess, you don't like it
when things get too clingy.

502
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:33,541
- Exactly.
- Right? Same here, most of the time.

503
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:36,544
- It's all about space, right?
- Exactly. Space is important.

504
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:38,045
- It's about breathing room.
- True that.

505
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:40,131
So maybe seeing each other
only on weekends would work.

506
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:42,133
- Yeah, maybe.
- That'd be easy, right?

507
00:21:42,134 --> 00:21:44,760
That way, we don't have to stick our noses
into each other's business.

508
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:46,095
For sure. That'd be good.

509
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,847
- We're kinda similar, huh?
- Yeah.

510
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:50,266
So what now?

511
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:52,101
Yikes, bail, bail, bail, bail.

512
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:54,979
What? Don't bail on me!

513
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:59,150
Me and Ryopi were just cracking up
the whole time, talking about crude stuff.

514
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,485
Just when we start having
a real conversation,

515
00:22:01,486 --> 00:22:02,987
one of us starts joking around.

516
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:05,573
He's just so easy to talk to. Seriously.

517
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:07,659
He might actually be interesting.

518
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:11,620
So that was my first
one-on-one conversation with Sara.

519
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:14,457
And, yeah,
it was really comfortable talking to her.

520
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:17,752
We just really clicked.
You never know until you give it a shot.

521
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:20,463
Now that we've talked, I'm starting
to see her in a different light.

522
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:22,965
- Oh, that's good.
- Wait, was that their first one-on-one?

523
00:22:22,966 --> 00:22:24,050
I think so.

524
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:25,468
- First real chat?
- Yes, their first.

525
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:26,761
They look good together.

526
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,720
- Right.
- Don't they?

527
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:29,889
Watching this show makes me realize

528
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:32,308
people change so much
depending on who they're with.

529
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:33,309
- Mmm.
- That's true.

530
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:36,520
Different sides of their personalities
emerge, they can be so different.

531
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:39,023
We were seeing
a version of her we've never seen.

532
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,775
- Yes.
- And with Ryopi.

533
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:43,778
But then again,
she knows Kazuma's still there.

534
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:46,280
She knows he's had a thing for her
since day one.

535
00:22:46,281 --> 00:22:47,615
The guy is so devoted.

536
00:22:47,616 --> 00:22:48,908
But, you know,

537
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:52,203
I still can't help but feel like
she was more herself with Ryopi.

538
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:55,081
- That's true.
- Wow, the action finally begins.

539
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,040
- Love it.
- Mmm.

540
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:59,460
- Just in time for the show to wrap up.
- How many episodes are left?

541
00:22:59,461 --> 00:23:01,962
We're deep into the second half already.
We have two episodes left.

542
00:23:01,963 --> 00:23:04,548
- Two episodes?
- So they have to go bam, bam, bam.

543
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:06,635
- How much can this develop?
- That's what I'm saying.

544
00:23:08,053 --> 00:23:11,056
- Can we talk?
- Uh, sure, okay.

545
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,641
- I wanted to apologize first.
- Okay.

546
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:14,725
I really screwed up.

547
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:17,353
No, don't worry about it at all.

548
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:19,439
There's a lot going on, so it's okay.

549
00:23:20,023 --> 00:23:22,441
- Like, when you were leaving the school…
- Yeah.

550
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:25,820
When I thought I might not get to see you
anymore, I felt like all I could do was…

551
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:27,113
what I did back there.

552
00:23:27,114 --> 00:23:30,282
You wrote that in your letter too,
about what happened during Part 1.

553
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:31,992
I put myself out there like that

554
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:35,579
because I wanted to make my feelings
clear to you even just a little.

555
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,331
Whether that was the right move or not…

556
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:38,249
Right.

557
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:39,792
…that's for you to decide.

558
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:40,709
Mmm-hmm.

559
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:43,963
I just felt I owed you an apology
before anything else.

560
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:47,216
- So I'm sorry.
- Mmm, it's totally fine. I'm okay with it.

561
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:48,051
- Thanks.
- Yeah.

562
00:23:48,635 --> 00:23:50,469
- You have fun on the date?
- Well…

563
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:52,012
- You mean with Rune?
- Uh-huh.

564
00:23:52,013 --> 00:23:54,932
The setting was something
totally different, so yeah.

565
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,101
It was fun in a way, but, hmm…

566
00:23:57,102 --> 00:24:00,312
To be honest, I'm interested in you,
but I'm interested in Rune too.

567
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,230
Mmm.

568
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:03,774
I went on that date,
but I wasn't sure how I felt.

569
00:24:03,775 --> 00:24:05,568
- Sure.
- So I was just nervous the whole time.

570
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:08,612
I felt like
I finally started to relax at the end.

571
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:10,115
Well, I still really like you.

572
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:15,871
Yeah, I know that.

573
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,706
And we don't have much time to talk.

574
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:20,499
- That's a problem.
- There's a lot going on.

575
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,625
But the reality is…

576
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:24,379
- "Reality" is a scary word.
- Yeah. But for real, um…

577
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:27,757
I'm gonna keep taking
everything I learned in Part 1

578
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:30,718
and try my best to apply it here.

579
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:31,635
Uh-huh.

580
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:34,139
I'm just gonna keep putting
my honest feelings out there.

581
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:36,766
- So, yeah.
- All right, I gotcha.

582
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:41,020
Even when he says all that,
she's like, "Okay."

583
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:43,063
- She's so reserved.
- Maybe she's just shy.

584
00:24:43,064 --> 00:24:44,023
That's what I thought.

585
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:47,234
Maybe she's always had trouble
expressing her true feelings.

586
00:24:47,235 --> 00:24:48,319
LOVE DINER

587
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:50,238
- Hey there.
- Whoa.

588
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:53,700
- I've been waiting for you.
- What's up?

589
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:56,619
Wow, it's kinda… kinda crazy.

590
00:24:56,620 --> 00:24:58,996
- Mimi sure is popular.
- She is.

591
00:24:58,997 --> 00:25:01,707
She's kinda the prom queen, right?
Of course she is.

592
00:25:01,708 --> 00:25:03,167
SHARAN (21)
LOUNGE HOSTESS

593
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,878
I guess everyone loves that kinda of face.

594
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:08,422
- Right?
- It's not just about her looks.

595
00:25:08,423 --> 00:25:09,591
It's what's inside too.

596
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:12,552
So…

597
00:25:14,095 --> 00:25:16,515
does that mean
Mimi is the only one for you now?

598
00:25:18,141 --> 00:25:19,309
The one on your mind?

599
00:25:19,935 --> 00:25:21,102
Mmm…

600
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:25,982
Yeah, my feelings for her
still haven't changed. Not at all.

601
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:30,945
All right, then.

602
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:31,780
Mmm.

603
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:40,038
- So, what exactly do you like about Mimi?
- You really asking?

604
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,291
Well, Mimi is, uh…

605
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:47,002
really straightforward,
you know, as a person.

606
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:50,548
She's the kind of woman who makes you
notice things you wouldn't otherwise.

607
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:52,551
- Mmm-hmm.
- She's so present, you know?

608
00:25:53,176 --> 00:25:56,595
When I'm around her, she makes me alive
to the world in a different way.

609
00:25:56,596 --> 00:25:59,265
I feel like she makes me
see things clearly somehow.

610
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:00,392
Mmm.

611
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:04,353
So it's not about her having
a pretty face or anything like that.

612
00:26:04,354 --> 00:26:06,855
- It's about who she is.
- Mmm-hmm, yeah.

613
00:26:06,856 --> 00:26:09,609
That's what usually
draws me closer to someone.

614
00:26:10,193 --> 00:26:13,529
Yeah, like,
someone grounded on the inside.

615
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:15,197
- Mmm…
- Yeah.

616
00:26:15,198 --> 00:26:16,283
That's what you like.

617
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:22,121
Well, obviously, I can tell
that's where your heart is now.

618
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:23,081
So, yeah…

619
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:28,544
I'll give you up then.

620
00:26:28,545 --> 00:26:29,588
- Mmm.
- Yeah.

621
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:31,881
Completely.

622
00:26:33,091 --> 00:26:33,967
All right?

623
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:36,427
I mean, I'm totally out now.

624
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:38,054
- Hmm?
- So thanks.

625
00:26:38,763 --> 00:26:40,515
- Are you--
- I'm done, so…

626
00:26:41,224 --> 00:26:44,019
Mmm-hmm. It's no big deal anymore.

627
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:47,230
- Thanks, though.
- Good night.

628
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:53,153
Bye-bye.

629
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:04,955
She kept saying, "I'm done, I'm out."

630
00:27:04,956 --> 00:27:07,207
- That was a little…
- Yeah, she still has feelings.

631
00:27:07,208 --> 00:27:09,752
- Tai-chan has no feelings for her at all.
- Yeah.

632
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:12,921
I think she came over to confirm that,
which was a brave move.

633
00:27:12,922 --> 00:27:15,799
And Tai-chan, I don't think
he could've done that in Part 1.

634
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:17,676
- No, no way.
- He's changed.

635
00:27:17,677 --> 00:27:21,639
He probably said all that so he could
help Sharan find what she's looking for.

636
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:22,723
- Mmm.
- Good point.

637
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,476
- Takes guts.
- I mean, what he likes about Mimi.

638
00:27:28,355 --> 00:27:31,065
- Kazuma, how's it going? Making progress?
- This guy's a wizard.

639
00:27:31,066 --> 00:27:33,525
- Mmm-hmm, I've gotten pretty far.
- That's looking good.

640
00:27:33,526 --> 00:27:34,569
That's impressive.

641
00:27:35,528 --> 00:27:37,363
If you have time, can you draw one for me?

642
00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:38,364
Yeah.

643
00:27:38,365 --> 00:27:40,574
I don't know.
I'm on a tight schedule here, buddy.

644
00:27:40,575 --> 00:27:42,284
I got no time.

645
00:27:42,285 --> 00:27:43,952
- For real?
- That's awesome!

646
00:27:43,953 --> 00:27:46,705
- He's drawing this for Sara, remember?
- That's the one he's giving to her.

647
00:27:46,706 --> 00:27:48,040
- Yeah.
- Right.

648
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:49,875
Giving me the cold shoulder?

649
00:27:49,876 --> 00:27:52,378
- Oh, wow.
- You're good.

650
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:54,588
- You've made a lot of progress.
- That's dope.

651
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:56,256
He's in the zone.

652
00:27:56,257 --> 00:27:57,466
- Hold on.
- What?

653
00:27:57,467 --> 00:27:58,717
- What now?
- Come on!

654
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:00,219
- What is it?
- What the hell?

655
00:28:00,220 --> 00:28:03,180
- Everyone's like, "What now?"
- <i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

656
00:28:03,181 --> 00:28:04,348
Morning.

657
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:06,266
<i>Only four days until the confession.</i>

658
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:07,643
We know.

659
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:11,188
<i>The men will ask out
the women they're interested in.</i>

660
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:12,899
<i>Get to know them better.</i>

661
00:28:13,483 --> 00:28:16,236
Here comes Kazuma.

662
00:28:16,736 --> 00:28:20,489
<i>Using the PA system,
the men will announce their choice.</i>

663
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:23,534
<i>Choose wisely.
This may be your last chance.</i>

664
00:28:23,535 --> 00:28:28,164
<i>In the event that a woman
is chosen by more than one man,</i>

665
00:28:28,707 --> 00:28:30,999
<i>she should meet with the one who she wants</i>

666
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:34,002
<i>to build
a deeper emotional connection with.</i>

667
00:28:34,003 --> 00:28:35,212
I don't like this!

668
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:37,256
- Why are you looking at me?
- Good luck choosing.

669
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,299
- No, no, no, no.
- <i>Oh, it's this one.</i>

670
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,844
<i>Yeah, here it is.</i>

671
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:46,098
Calling girls out with the school's
PA system? This is nerve-wracking.

672
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:47,851
- This is good.
- Yeah, this is a good one.

673
00:28:59,946 --> 00:29:00,780
All right.

674
00:29:01,531 --> 00:29:04,283
<i>Kamaken's choice is gonna be
obvious. They've been pretty steady.</i>

675
00:29:04,284 --> 00:29:07,369
<i>I hope you're right.</i>

676
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:09,329
- <i>Check, check.</i>
- Kazuma?

677
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:11,291
<i>Yo, mic check, one-two.</i>

678
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:13,793
- Not Kazuma.
- Is it Ryopi?

679
00:29:14,377 --> 00:29:15,461
It's Kamaken.

680
00:29:15,462 --> 00:29:17,880
Oh, really?

681
00:29:17,881 --> 00:29:20,091
- <i>Oh! She wants the invite.</i>
- <i>Nice. Yeah.</i>

682
00:29:20,675 --> 00:29:21,509
So, today,

683
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:24,720
the person I want to talk to is…

684
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:27,390
This is scary.

685
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:35,481
…Rinrin.

686
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:37,817
<i>I'll be in our room.</i>

687
00:29:38,401 --> 00:29:40,235
- Oh, it's the guys' room.
- <i>Come on over.</i>

688
00:29:40,236 --> 00:29:41,653
<i>All right, peace.</i>

689
00:29:41,654 --> 00:29:43,405
- All right, peace!
- Peace out!

690
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:45,282
Aw, the look on her face!

691
00:29:45,283 --> 00:29:46,825
- Rinrin's adorable.
- She's so cute.

692
00:29:46,826 --> 00:29:48,702
- Her dimples are adorable.
- That smile.

693
00:29:48,703 --> 00:29:50,913
- I'm so happy!
- This is freaky!

694
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:52,081
This is nerve-wracking.

695
00:29:53,082 --> 00:29:54,292
I'm kinda mortified.

696
00:29:57,712 --> 00:29:58,546
ON AIR

697
00:30:00,340 --> 00:30:02,508
Check, check. Hey.

698
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:04,302
Uh, this is Kazuma.

699
00:30:07,013 --> 00:30:09,682
So, the girl I want to talk to today is…

700
00:30:10,850 --> 00:30:11,976
<i>Who could it be?</i>

701
00:30:14,562 --> 00:30:15,479
…Sara.

702
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:18,190
I'll be waiting for you
at the smoking area on the second floor.

703
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:21,276
- Smoking area, interesting.
- He's so funny.

704
00:30:21,277 --> 00:30:23,195
<i>That will be all.</i>

705
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:24,905
Just like a teacher.

706
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:26,990
He's always so funny. Oh, my gosh.

707
00:30:26,991 --> 00:30:29,451
How does he always manage
to lighten the mood?

708
