- Mmm… Mmm…

922
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:45,668
Yeah, he may or may not have kissed me.

923
00:41:45,669 --> 00:41:48,963
- I don't know, man.
- But that was well before I showed up.

924
00:41:48,964 --> 00:41:50,256
- Yeah, it was.
- Uh-huh.

925
00:41:50,257 --> 00:41:52,967
Yeah, I've been meaning
to tell you about that, but…

926
00:41:52,968 --> 00:41:54,928
I don't mind at all, no big deal.

927
00:41:54,929 --> 00:41:56,180
- I'm glad to hear that.
- For sure.

928
00:41:56,764 --> 00:41:58,848
- I was like, "Oh, that happened."
- Right.

929
00:41:58,849 --> 00:42:00,558
Like this? Lips to lips?

930
00:42:00,559 --> 00:42:02,769
Mmm, I guess.

931
00:42:02,770 --> 00:42:04,980
- It also happened right here.
- No way.

932
00:42:08,108 --> 00:42:09,193
That's so funny.

933
00:42:10,110 --> 00:42:12,029
So should I kiss you on the cheek?

934
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:16,074
I don't know, I'm kinda shy.

935
00:42:16,075 --> 00:42:18,743
If you want me to, I'll do it.
On the cheek, though.

936
00:42:18,744 --> 00:42:19,662
Then do it.

937
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:29,629
No, no, I'm so embarrassed.

938
00:42:29,630 --> 00:42:31,047
<i>Nice, nice, nice.</i>

939
00:42:31,048 --> 00:42:32,799
<i>You can tell they're comfortable.</i>

940
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,635
The man's gotta take the first step.

941
00:42:36,595 --> 00:42:38,888
I wasn't gonna do it
if you said you were too embarrassed,

942
00:42:38,889 --> 00:42:40,431
but you gave the green light.

943
00:42:40,432 --> 00:42:42,976
- So I had to follow through.
- Oof, my brain's not working right now.

944
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:45,437
What should I do?
I feel like, "Ooh, ooh, ooh."

945
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:52,402
You sleepy?

946
00:42:52,403 --> 00:42:54,279
LADIES

947
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,905
- Oh, man.
- Have fun.

948
00:42:55,906 --> 00:42:57,908
- Enjoy yourself.
- Good luck.

949
00:42:58,492 --> 00:43:01,744
I wonder where she's headed.
My sweet big sis, Sara.

950
00:43:01,745 --> 00:43:03,037
- Bye, babes.
- Bye-bye.

951
00:43:03,038 --> 00:43:04,456
- Bye, Sara.
- See you later.

952
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:09,628
Well, guys,
Little Kaho is going to turn in.

953
00:43:10,212 --> 00:43:13,756
I'm going to dream about
getting picked by all the guys here.

954
00:43:13,757 --> 00:43:16,175
- <i>Tough to not be chosen at all.</i>
- <i>Poor girls.</i>

955
00:43:16,176 --> 00:43:18,637
<i>Yeah, especially after
being here for this long.</i>

956
00:43:35,654 --> 00:43:37,864
<i>No!</i>

957
00:43:37,865 --> 00:43:40,159
Come on, don't do that to him!

958
00:43:48,792 --> 00:43:50,669
Oh. I knew it.

959
00:43:52,004 --> 00:43:53,755
<i>Yes!</i>

960
00:43:53,756 --> 00:43:55,506
Yes!

961
00:43:55,507 --> 00:43:57,216
Oh, my God!

962
00:43:57,217 --> 00:44:00,219
- Is it awkward to sit right next to you?
- No, it's fine. I don't mind.

963
00:44:00,220 --> 00:44:01,512
- After you.
- With your permission.

964
00:44:01,513 --> 00:44:04,140
I was trying to entertain myself.

965
00:44:04,141 --> 00:44:06,142
I gotta say, I was so surprised.

966
00:44:06,143 --> 00:44:07,853
- Thought you'd be.
- The girls' room was buzzing.

967
00:44:08,437 --> 00:44:09,812
- Oh, really?
- Seriously.

968
00:44:09,813 --> 00:44:13,274
- I was buzzing doing the announcement.
- I bet. Everyone was shocked.

969
00:44:13,275 --> 00:44:14,776
- Like, "Oh, what?"
- Yeah.

970
00:44:14,777 --> 00:44:16,110
- I can imagine.
- Mmm.

971
00:44:16,111 --> 00:44:18,988
The reason I decided to come to you
is 'cause I wanted to tell you…

972
00:44:18,989 --> 00:44:22,909
I mean, I know we've only talked
a little bit up to this point, right?

973
00:44:22,910 --> 00:44:23,826
Twice.

974
00:44:23,827 --> 00:44:25,620
But I realized
what a good listener you are.

975
00:44:25,621 --> 00:44:27,622
- You pick up on the way I'm feeling.
- Aw, thanks.

976
00:44:27,623 --> 00:44:30,083
And I've never really
experienced that before.

977
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:31,876
- I just--
- Yeah, we have a lot in common too.

978
00:44:31,877 --> 00:44:33,503
- Mmm, I know, right?
- Yeah.

979
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:36,673
- Turns out we're similar.
- For sure, we think the same way.

980
00:44:36,674 --> 00:44:39,425
We value our space
and don't want things to get too clingy.

981
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:41,052
- Yeah, exactly.
- I think you understand me.

982
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:43,554
And in the end,
it made me decide to come to you.

983
00:44:43,555 --> 00:44:44,390
- Gotcha.
- Right.

984
00:44:45,182 --> 00:44:48,184
Yeah. After yesterday,
I definitely think we're compatible.

985
00:44:48,185 --> 00:44:50,436
Yeah. I just like talking to you the most.

986
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:52,730
- Well, yeah, only--
- What?

987
00:44:52,731 --> 00:44:54,148
I mean, I agree.

988
00:44:54,149 --> 00:44:57,110
But there are a few people
I feel comfortable with here.

989
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:58,653
- I like talking to Rinrin too.
- Sure.

990
00:44:58,654 --> 00:45:02,448
Yeah, Rinrin's fun to be around,
but I feel like I'm doing all the talking.

991
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:03,700
But that sense of ease…

992
00:45:03,701 --> 00:45:04,701
- With me?
- Yeah.

993
00:45:04,702 --> 00:45:06,744
- Your sense of calmness and ease.
- Yeah.

994
00:45:06,745 --> 00:45:07,955
That's what really struck me.

995
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:11,958
Man, you're so funny.

996
00:45:11,959 --> 00:45:13,418
No, but the other thing is,

997
00:45:13,419 --> 00:45:16,713
I do feel kinda bad for Kazuma
because, um,

998
00:45:16,714 --> 00:45:18,798
he's, like, making you a drawing.

999
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:21,801
- Yeah, that's been a big thing, right?
- Right. Oh, yeah.

1000
00:45:21,802 --> 00:45:23,636
That's why I thought
I wouldn't get picked.

1001
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:24,804
- Oh, did you?
- Mmm.

1002
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:27,432
- Yeah, we all see him drawing for you.
- Right, yeah.

1003
00:45:27,433 --> 00:45:30,685
- Wow, am I doing something shitty?
- Well, if you are, so am I.

1004
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:33,396
- Yeah, we're both responsible, no doubt.
- We both have blood on our hands.

1005
00:45:33,397 --> 00:45:36,900
Yeah, from here on out,
it's a head-to-head battle with Kazuma.

1006
00:45:41,196 --> 00:45:42,447
Poor Kazuma!

1007
00:45:42,448 --> 00:45:43,740
But they're accomplices now.

1008
00:45:43,741 --> 00:45:45,241
- Psychologically speaking.
- Yeah, true.

1009
00:45:45,242 --> 00:45:47,577
- That might heat up.
- Being partners in crime is the best fuel

1010
00:45:47,578 --> 00:45:49,412
for their romantic fire, right?

1011
00:45:49,413 --> 00:45:52,331
I hope Kazuma gets wise to that soon
and goes to Kahochi.

1012
00:45:52,332 --> 00:45:55,126
- I know, Kahochi still has a chance.
- I think she does.

1013
00:45:55,127 --> 00:45:56,669
- Yeah.
- She's started a little behind…

1014
00:45:56,670 --> 00:45:58,713
- But we don't know what might happen.
- Yeah.

1015
00:45:58,714 --> 00:46:00,214
- What you doing?
- Where's he?

1016
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:02,633
- I don't know.
- This is insane, right?

1017
00:46:02,634 --> 00:46:04,761
She's with Tai-chan now, but, you know,

1018
00:46:04,762 --> 00:46:08,097
first, she walked past Maru
then right past me.

1019
00:46:08,098 --> 00:46:09,640
- You saw her too?
- It sucked.

1020
00:46:09,641 --> 00:46:10,767
That's tough.

1021
00:46:10,768 --> 00:46:12,602
Yikes.

1022
00:46:12,603 --> 00:46:15,021
- That hurts. I bet you're pissed, huh?
- Yeah.

1023
00:46:15,022 --> 00:46:17,524
- That messes with your head.
- Sorry, guys.

1024
00:46:18,025 --> 00:46:19,859
- I don't like it.
- Should we do something?

1025
00:46:19,860 --> 00:46:22,236
- I wouldn't do that.
- You wouldn't, right?

1026
00:46:22,237 --> 00:46:23,863
- Definitely not.
- Let's make something.

1027
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:25,449
- We can do that.
- What should we make?

1028
00:46:30,037 --> 00:46:31,037
Hmm…

1029
00:46:31,038 --> 00:46:34,582
Would you mind
if I go sort out my thoughts a little?

1030
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:36,042
- Sure, of course.
- Okay.

1031
00:46:36,043 --> 00:46:37,835
- I gotcha.
- I get it.

1032
00:46:37,836 --> 00:46:39,504
- Take your time.
- Thanks.

1033
00:46:39,505 --> 00:46:40,838
- Mmm.
- Good idea.

1034
00:46:40,839 --> 00:46:43,591
- Sorry about that.
- It's okay. It's all good.

1035
00:46:43,592 --> 00:46:45,677
We're all feeling like crap anyway.

1036
00:47:02,945 --> 00:47:06,907
HEAD OVER HEELS

1037
00:47:16,834 --> 00:47:18,918
- <i>What's she doing?</i>
- <i>Where's she going?</i>

1038
00:47:18,919 --> 00:47:20,629
- <i>She's taking her purse.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

1039
00:47:24,049 --> 00:47:24,967
<i>Huh?</i>

1040
00:47:27,052 --> 00:47:29,220
<i>She's going to the gate.</i>

1041
00:47:29,221 --> 00:47:30,305
<i>And then?</i>

1042
00:47:32,599 --> 00:47:34,810
- Wait… What?
- Uh…

1043
00:47:36,937 --> 00:47:38,980
So I guess she picked Tai-chan.

1044
00:47:38,981 --> 00:47:41,358
- Are you shocked and sad?
- Yeah.

1045
00:47:42,109 --> 00:47:44,068
I kind of expected her
to go with Tai-chan,

1046
00:47:44,069 --> 00:47:47,113
but to be honest, your announcement
was pretty unexpected as well.

1047
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:48,030
How so?

1048
00:47:48,031 --> 00:47:50,283
I mean, all the girls were like, "Really?"

1049
00:47:50,284 --> 00:47:52,410
- About the person I chose?
- Yeah, yeah.

1050
00:47:52,411 --> 00:47:54,621
- Uh-huh.
- But I gotta say, I saw it coming.

1051
00:47:56,081 --> 00:47:58,541
- Oh, you did? Interesting.
- Yeah, so it wasn't a huge thing.

1052
00:47:58,542 --> 00:47:59,376
I didn't…

1053
00:48:00,460 --> 00:48:01,461
feel too hurt.

1054
00:48:02,170 --> 00:48:03,547
I wasn't down in the dumps.

1055
00:48:05,799 --> 00:48:06,799
SHARAN, RINRIN, KAHOCHI

1056
00:48:06,800 --> 00:48:09,552
Finishing touches. We gotta wait
for the right moment to show these.

1057
00:48:09,553 --> 00:48:12,097
- Surprise. That what you meant?
- Yeah.

1058
00:48:12,681 --> 00:48:14,307
That's so nice.

1059
00:48:14,308 --> 00:48:16,935
Oh, my God, they'll definitely
be happy to see these.

1060
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:20,439
Oh, it's looking good. Wow, isn't it cute?

1061
00:48:21,106 --> 00:48:23,734
Oh, that's incredible. You're a genius.

1062
00:48:24,484 --> 00:48:29,447
Check it out. It's all about getting
that handcrafted touch, you know?

1063
00:48:29,448 --> 00:48:31,950
- Beautiful. Aren't these amazing?
- They're nice.

1064
00:48:33,076 --> 00:48:36,245
Wait, these look better than I expected.
They're awesome, huh?

1065
00:48:36,246 --> 00:48:38,372
It's all about nailing the presentation.

1066
00:48:38,373 --> 00:48:40,292
<i>So pretty!</i>

1067
00:48:40,959 --> 00:48:42,835
- I'm speechless!
- Is this a bakery?

1068
00:48:42,836 --> 00:48:45,254
Even a cake shop
couldn't make something like this.

1069
00:48:45,255 --> 00:48:46,631
Maru and his baking skills…

1070
00:48:46,632 --> 00:48:47,965
No kidding.

1071
00:48:47,966 --> 00:48:50,343
- His talent is just…
- Blossoming.

1072
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:51,594
- It's blossoming, right?
- 100%!

1073
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:53,179
It wasn't romance or a girl.

1074
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:54,680
- It was baking!
- Yes!

1075
00:48:54,681 --> 00:48:57,350
- That's what he found here.
- He found a passion for cakes.

1076
00:48:57,351 --> 00:48:59,185
- He's a pastry chef.
- Pastry chef! Both are!

1077
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:01,687
Hang on. This is a reality dating show,
not a job fair.

1078
00:49:01,688 --> 00:49:04,774
"The social reintegration project:
Find your career here."

1079
00:49:04,775 --> 00:49:06,443
That's more like it.

1080
00:49:07,235 --> 00:49:09,528
- Where did Sharan go, anyway?
- Sharan?

1081
00:49:09,529 --> 00:49:10,655
Yeah.

1082
00:49:10,656 --> 00:49:12,907
She might want
to be alone with her thoughts

1083
00:49:12,908 --> 00:49:14,952
'cause of Tai-chan's announcement.

1084
00:49:23,001 --> 00:49:24,293
<i>All right, everyone.</i>

1085
00:49:24,294 --> 00:49:28,297
<i>Let's continue preparations
for the locals' thank-you party.</i>

1086
00:49:28,298 --> 00:49:29,674
I'm gonna paint here too.

1087
00:49:29,675 --> 00:49:31,300
- Yeah.
- Leave some for us, though.

1088
00:49:31,301 --> 00:49:34,178
Why don't you leave
this part on the left side?

1089
00:49:34,179 --> 00:49:36,138
- Okay.
- Okay. For Kamaken?

1090
00:49:36,139 --> 00:49:37,723
No, Mimi said
she wanted to paint a little.

1091
00:49:37,724 --> 00:49:39,225
- Really? It's kinda--
- Yeah.

1092
00:49:39,226 --> 00:49:41,143
- Wow, the paint's out!
- We're painting.

1093
00:49:41,144 --> 00:49:43,020
We're trying to get the first coat on.

1094
00:49:43,021 --> 00:49:44,939
I was gonna go change real quick.

1095
00:49:44,940 --> 00:49:46,857
- Nice. Go ahead and change.
- All good?

1096
00:49:46,858 --> 00:49:48,192
- I wanna try.
- Looking good.

1097
00:49:48,193 --> 00:49:49,860
- No idea what I'm doing.
- Nice. Suits you.

1098
00:49:49,861 --> 00:49:52,154
- Same. Just pretend.
- How do you do it?

1099
00:49:52,155 --> 00:49:54,156
- Come here.
- Like Picasso.

1100
00:49:54,157 --> 00:49:56,075
Don't spread it too thin.

1101
00:49:56,076 --> 00:49:58,285
- Paint the parts you like for now.
- Too much?

1102
00:49:58,286 --> 00:49:59,496
- Really?
- Just like that.

1103
00:50:01,123 --> 00:50:02,581
Good work. Nice.

1104
00:50:02,582 --> 00:50:05,376
- Don't get in the way. Stop it!
- Don't mess around!

1105
00:50:05,377 --> 00:50:07,336
- Can I borrow Kazuma for a second?
- Sure.

1106
00:50:07,337 --> 00:50:08,421
Kazuma, let's talk.

1107
00:50:08,422 --> 00:50:09,839
- Let's go for a smoke.
- Oh, sure.

1108
00:50:09,840 --> 00:50:11,758
<i>He wants to do the right thing.</i>

1109
00:50:15,804 --> 00:50:18,974
Yeah, so there's something
I want to talk to you about.

1110
00:50:19,641 --> 00:50:20,475
What is it?

1111
00:50:21,768 --> 00:50:24,521
Well, look, obviously,
you know that Sara came to see me.

1112
00:50:26,106 --> 00:50:27,898
And I know about your feelings for her,

1113
00:50:27,899 --> 00:50:30,652
so, you know, I don't want
to get in the way of that.

1114
00:50:31,445 --> 00:50:34,822
Well, I don't need pity or compassion
when it comes to her--

1115
00:50:34,823 --> 00:50:36,407
It's not about me pitying you.

1116
00:50:36,408 --> 00:50:39,076
This isn't me
trying to stir up trouble or anything.

1117
00:50:39,077 --> 00:50:41,120
I just wanted
to get in front of it and be honest.

1118
00:50:41,121 --> 00:50:43,080
Gotcha. Thanks for clearing that up.

1119
00:50:43,081 --> 00:50:45,042
I don't have any reason to be angry.

1120
00:50:46,918 --> 00:50:49,755
Well, then, I guess
it's <i>Badly In Love</i> from here on out.

1121
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:54,384
- So you're going for her now?
- Uh-huh.

1122
00:50:56,344 --> 00:50:58,012
Well, she might've picked you today,

1123
00:50:58,013 --> 00:51:00,931
but I plan to keep pushing
until the last minute.

1124
00:51:00,932 --> 00:51:02,267
- Yeah.
- Just so you know.

1125
00:51:03,351 --> 00:51:07,104
Looks like I picked the most formidable
guy here as a rival, huh?

1126
00:51:07,105 --> 00:51:09,607
Yeah, I don't plan on losing.

1127
00:51:09,608 --> 00:51:12,235
- Let's do this.
- I'll need that competitive edge to win.

1128
00:51:13,653 --> 00:51:15,155
I just wanted to talk it out.

1129
00:51:17,949 --> 00:51:20,285
All right then, may the best man win.

1130
00:51:21,453 --> 00:51:23,496
I'm gonna charge ahead until the last day.

1131
00:51:23,497 --> 00:51:24,456
'Course you are.

1132
00:51:25,332 --> 00:51:28,209
I turned out to be a dark horse.

1133
00:51:28,210 --> 00:51:31,087
- I was surprised to see you here.
- Nice work!

1134
00:51:31,088 --> 00:51:32,546
Yay! It turned out okay!

1135
00:51:32,547 --> 00:51:33,839
- So cool!
- Watch out.

1136
00:51:33,840 --> 00:51:36,300
- Yikes!
- My gosh, close call.

1137
00:51:36,301 --> 00:51:38,385
- Super close.
- That's a relief.

1138
00:51:38,386 --> 00:51:41,347
- Give her some room.
- Wasn't like they'd fall apart.

1139
00:51:41,348 --> 00:51:43,516
Maru's taking another shot
at these burgers.

1140
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:44,517
Crazy, right?

1141
00:51:44,518 --> 00:51:47,478
If anyone asks, it's my signature dish.
"What are you making, Chef?"

1142
00:51:47,479 --> 00:51:51,065
"Hamburger steaks."
Gotta say it with a little attitude.

1143
00:51:51,066 --> 00:51:53,234
You've gotten a lot better
since the first day.

1144
00:51:53,235 --> 00:51:54,944
- It's crazy.
- Seriously.

1145
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:56,695
He's more confident too.

1146
00:51:56,696 --> 00:51:58,781
Dude is in the zone. Those look good.

1147
00:51:58,782 --> 00:52:01,243
- Right?
- Second time's the charm, I guess.

1148
00:52:02,035 --> 00:52:03,245
Nice, nice.

1149
00:52:04,746 --> 00:52:07,581
- Is Maru a genius?
- Yeah, a culinary genius.

1150
00:52:07,582 --> 00:52:10,292
I keep thinking
Ryopi and Maru should open a restaurant.

1151
00:52:10,293 --> 00:52:12,211
- Interesting idea.
- Ryopi can run it.

1152
00:52:12,212 --> 00:52:13,504
- He's the owner.
- The manager.

1153
00:52:13,505 --> 00:52:15,548
And Maru can give
his full attention to baking.

1154
00:52:15,549 --> 00:52:16,882
Ah.

1155
00:52:16,883 --> 00:52:20,136
- All cakes all the time.
- Maru would go, "Ryopi, I pick you."

1156
00:52:20,137 --> 00:52:21,595
- No, no.
- "Let's be partners in crime!"

1157
00:52:21,596 --> 00:52:23,430
- "We found each other!"
- You've corrupted Awich.

1158
00:52:23,431 --> 00:52:26,268
- They leave as a couple, right? So sweet.
- No, guys. Remember, dating show.

1159
00:52:26,852 --> 00:52:29,311
- Where'd Sharan go?
- Add water and you're done.

1160
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:31,105
- I have no idea.
- You're right. She's gone.

1161
00:52:31,106 --> 00:52:33,357
- We haven't seen Sharan.
- Sharan's not here.

1162
00:52:33,358 --> 00:52:35,109
- Why not?
- I don't know.

1163
00:52:35,110 --> 00:52:37,278
She wasn't around when we came in, right?

1164
00:52:37,279 --> 00:52:40,739
Um, yeah but she was with us
before we started working on the bench.

1165
00:52:40,740 --> 00:52:43,325
I think she said
she wanted to be alone for a bit.

1166
00:52:43,326 --> 00:52:45,287
- Okay.
- She said that and left.

1167
00:52:46,121 --> 00:52:47,913
- Should we be worried?
- What was wrong?

1168
00:52:47,914 --> 00:52:49,623
I thought about offering to go, but…

1169
00:52:49,624 --> 00:52:51,542
- Give her space.
- She want to be alone?

1170
00:52:51,543 --> 00:52:54,128
She said she wanted to be by herself,
so I didn't wanna follow her.

1171
00:52:54,129 --> 00:52:56,922
If she wanted to go home
or something, I'd try to talk to her,

1172
00:52:56,923 --> 00:53:01,093
but if she just needs a minute to think,
then maybe we should give her that space.

1173
00:53:01,094 --> 00:53:02,511
I respect it.

1174
00:53:02,512 --> 00:53:04,346
- Do it one by one.
- Hold on.

1175
00:53:04,347 --> 00:53:06,807
- I feel I should go.
- Big one's for the guys.

1176
00:53:06,808 --> 00:53:09,310
- Can I sit next to you?
- Yeah, go right ahead.

1177
00:53:09,311 --> 00:53:10,686
- These are for the girls.
- Give me.

1178
00:53:10,687 --> 00:53:12,646
Everyone seems on edge.

1179
00:53:12,647 --> 00:53:14,773
I feel like I should go look for Sharan.

1180
00:53:14,774 --> 00:53:16,650
- Napkins, anyone?
- I want to go too.

1181
00:53:16,651 --> 00:53:18,569
- I can go. I don't mind.
- Hmm…

1182
00:53:18,570 --> 00:53:20,779
Well, then I'll leave it to you, I guess.

1183
00:53:20,780 --> 00:53:23,157
- We can't all go.
- Kazuma, let's go for now.

1184
00:53:23,158 --> 00:53:24,909
- Let's go.
- We're counting on you.

1185
00:53:24,910 --> 00:53:26,827
- Eat. Go ahead and start.
- Yeah, eat.

1186
00:53:26,828 --> 00:53:28,954
- This might take a while.
- Yeah.

1187
00:53:28,955 --> 00:53:30,456
Well, we'll wait for you for a minute.

1188
00:53:30,457 --> 00:53:32,166
We don't know where she is, though.

1189
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:34,878
- You can eat. It's fine.
- Dig in while it's hot.

1190
00:53:37,422 --> 00:53:39,883
- Hello? Sharan?
- Are you here?

1191
00:53:40,675 --> 00:53:41,967
No sign of her.

1192
00:53:41,968 --> 00:53:43,970
- She isn't here?
- Huh.

1193
00:53:45,263 --> 00:53:46,097
Sharan?

1194
00:53:47,265 --> 00:53:49,267
- She's not here.
- She sleeping or something?

1195
00:53:51,144 --> 00:53:52,771
- She's not here?
- Nope.

1196
00:53:55,232 --> 00:53:56,191
Where is she?

1197
00:53:56,942 --> 00:53:58,651
Wait, was her purse there?

1198
00:53:58,652 --> 00:54:00,070
Sharan.

1199
00:54:02,989 --> 00:54:04,949
- Don't see her.
- No way.

1200
00:54:04,950 --> 00:54:06,326
- Huh? Where is she?
- Really?

1201
00:54:07,202 --> 00:54:09,578
There's a cake.
She's the one we're celebrating.

1202
00:54:09,579 --> 00:54:11,455
- Oh, you're right.
- Yeah.

1203
00:54:11,456 --> 00:54:13,124
Yeah, we're celebrating her today.

1204
00:54:15,043 --> 00:54:17,753
Did you find her? Any sign of her?

1205
00:54:17,754 --> 00:54:19,713
- Let's try the PA room.
- This is not like her.

1206
00:54:19,714 --> 00:54:22,049
- Go back to dinner.
- Can I go in first?

1207
00:54:22,050 --> 00:54:23,217
I'm going in first.

1208
00:54:23,218 --> 00:54:25,470
- You sure?
- I think a girl should go in first.

1209
00:54:27,764 --> 00:54:29,890
Sharan. Huh?

1210
00:54:29,891 --> 00:54:30,892
She's not here.

1211
00:54:31,768 --> 00:54:33,269
No way.

1212
00:54:33,270 --> 00:54:34,353
Not here either.

1213
00:54:34,354 --> 00:54:37,189
- Did we look over here?
- Where the hell is she?

1214
00:54:37,190 --> 00:54:39,024
- What the…
- What the hell?

1215
00:54:39,025 --> 00:54:40,818
You never know, I mean…

1216
00:54:40,819 --> 00:54:43,862
- We looked everywhere, couldn't find her.
- Are you serious?

1217
00:54:43,863 --> 00:54:46,240
We went all the way
to the back of the sauna, nothing.

1218
00:54:46,241 --> 00:54:48,409
- She vanished.
- She's not in our room?

1219
00:54:48,410 --> 00:54:50,869
- Nope, she wasn't there.
- She's not anywhere.

1220
00:54:50,870 --> 00:54:52,204
She wasn't in her bed.

1221
00:54:52,205 --> 00:54:53,539
- The gym?
- Really?

1222
00:54:53,540 --> 00:54:56,125
- No sign of her.
- She might have left the school.

1223
00:54:56,126 --> 00:54:58,377
- Dropped out?
- Went home?

1224
00:54:58,378 --> 00:55:00,504
- Went home?
- For real?

1225
00:55:00,505 --> 00:55:02,339
She talked to Tai-chan yesterday.

1226
00:55:02,340 --> 00:55:04,426
- Mmm.
- How was she then?

1227
00:55:07,470 --> 00:55:09,306
- How was she then?
- Yeah.

1228
00:55:10,348 --> 00:55:12,725
- Hmm…
- Should I say it? Is it hard to say?

1229
00:55:12,726 --> 00:55:16,604
No, I can say it. She was like,
"Thanks for everything up until now."

1230
00:55:17,272 --> 00:55:18,106
What?

1231
00:55:18,732 --> 00:55:21,567
She said something like,
"Thanks for everything up until now."

1232
00:55:21,568 --> 00:55:22,526
That's what she said.

1233
00:55:22,527 --> 00:55:23,361
But then…

1234
00:55:24,362 --> 00:55:25,697
we ended the conversation.

1235
00:55:26,531 --> 00:55:29,534
- Right. So you don't know either.
- Yeah.

1236
00:55:31,369 --> 00:55:33,912
- She must have dropped out, right?
- For real?

1237
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:36,081
- You're kidding.
- All of a sudden?

1238
00:55:36,082 --> 00:55:39,084
Sounds like
she's done telling Tai-chan how she feels.

1239
00:55:39,085 --> 00:55:40,919
Maybe she hinted at it to Tai-chan,

1240
00:55:40,920 --> 00:55:43,047
but how could she just leave
without telling any of us?

1241
00:55:43,048 --> 00:55:43,882
I don't know.

1242
00:55:44,883 --> 00:55:46,216
What the heck?

1243
00:55:46,217 --> 00:55:49,470
I mean, there's no rule
that says she has to tell everyone.

1244
00:55:49,471 --> 00:55:50,387
Right.

1245
00:55:50,388 --> 00:55:52,307
Nothing we can do about it, then.
